(2165311, 296930, 47117, '<td valign="top">Here is an excerpt from a website. I was a bit confused by this image because I remember KISS from the 70''s and not the 80''s. Seems I was correct. I researched the era and found this:  <b>""Kiss" returns. Yes, the rock group that thrilled fans and terrified their parents in the ''70s has reunited for a summer tour beginning June 28 in Detroit. The 40-something rockers haven''t played together since 1979."</b> Therefore, this image is really a DNMC.  KISS albums and such may have been listened to and prevelant in the 80''s, but the band itself was already diminished in the 70''s and from the 70''s.  You missed it by one year. I still like the image though, and will give it a 5 for technicals and effort.</td>', 'Here is an excerpt from a website. I was a bit confused by this image because I remember KISS from the 70''s and not the 80''s. Seems I was correct. I researched the era and found this:  ""Kiss" returns. Yes, the rock group that thrilled fans and terrified their parents in the ''70s has reunited for a summer tour beginning June 28 in Detroit. The 40-something rockers haven''t played together since 1979." Therefore, this image is really a DNMC.  KISS albums and such may have been listened to and prevelant in the 80''s, but the band itself was already diminished in the 70''s and from the 70''s.  You missed it by one year. I still like the image though, and will give it a 5 for technicals and effort.', '2006-02-20 08:35:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2165319, 297639, 47117, '<td valign="top">There are a lot of Rubic''s Cubes in this challenge, but unfortunately, although some may have played with it in the 80''s, it was really created in 1975.  Therefore, the cube was really a 1970''s craze, and not an 80''s craze.<b>Rubik''s Cube was developed in 1975 by Ernö Rubik, a Hungarian professor of mathematics</b></td>', 'There are a lot of Rubic''s Cubes in this challenge, but unfortunately, although some may have played with it in the 80''s, it was really created in 1975.  Therefore, the cube was really a 1970''s craze, and not an 80''s craze.Rubik''s Cube was developed in 1975 by Ernö Rubik, a Hungarian professor of mathematics', '2006-02-20 08:40:39.000000', NULL, 1),
