(2172188, 296388, 3032, '<td valign="top">Oh man, it was so cool. I remember the day (must have been 6 or 7) when the first guy at school got a walkman for christmass. We all wanted one. <br/>Now with an itsy bitsy tiny mp3 player, able to hold 50+ 90 minute casettes and able to find your fav song within 10 seconds.... In 20 years we connect a wire to an unused part of our brain and upload the whole world database. :)</td>', 'Oh man, it was so cool. I remember the day (must have been 6 or 7) when the first guy at school got a walkman for christmass. We all wanted one. Now with an itsy bitsy tiny mp3 player, able to hold 50+ 90 minute casettes and able to find your fav song within 10 seconds.... In 20 years we connect a wire to an unused part of our brain and upload the whole world database. :)', '2006-02-22 13:53:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2172268, 297371, 3032, '<td valign="top">I like the idea and the way the light falls as a a spot with the lines and strong shadow on the background.<br/>However to my liking there is too much bleu/magenta tone in this photo. It takes the pop out of the skin colors and especially the hand looks a bit weird that way. When I do a quick correction with a white levels sampler on one of the bright parts of the breasts section it looks a bit more natural. Also a slight pull upwards on the curves makes it pop a little more and some mild sharpening 80% .3px on the creases in the dress makes the contrast of the edges a little better there.<br/>Posewise it looks like she is a bit shy. The arm in front of her body and the face looking away hidden by all that hair makes it look that way. It does make for a good shadow profile tough. The film poster is like that too, so it is not hones to critisize on that, altough Kim Basinger poses more toward the viewer. 7<br/> <br/>I''m looking forward to the workshop Gary. :)<br/>(Philos told me after I guessed his one right in one attempt and yours in one out of four)</td>', 'I like the idea and the way the light falls as a a spot with the lines and strong shadow on the background.However to my liking there is too much bleu/magenta tone in this photo. It takes the pop out of the skin colors and especially the hand looks a bit weird that way. When I do a quick correction with a white levels sampler on one of the bright parts of the breasts section it looks a bit more natural. Also a slight pull upwards on the curves makes it pop a little more and some mild sharpening 80% .3px on the creases in the dress makes the contrast of the edges a little better there.Posewise it looks like she is a bit shy. The arm in front of her body and the face looking away hidden by all that hair makes it look that way. It does make for a good shadow profile tough. The film poster is like that too, so it is not hones to critisize on that, altough Kim Basinger poses more toward the viewer. 7 I''m looking forward to the workshop Gary. :)(Philos told me after I guessed his one right in one attempt and yours in one out of four)', '2006-02-22 14:14:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2172319, 297815, 3032, '<td valign="top">Cool perspective and altough the chalk lines are not punk at all (as far as I know) they do enhance that punk feeling. 9<br/> <br/>Sonifo?</td>', 'Cool perspective and altough the chalk lines are not punk at all (as far as I know) they do enhance that punk feeling. 9 Sonifo?', '2006-02-22 14:23:34.000000', NULL, 1),
