(2181271, 297815, 16046, '<td valign="top">Well done, excellent color, great model.</td>', 'Well done, excellent color, great model.', '2006-02-25 02:18:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181282, 296930, 16046, '<td valign="top">should win, great image, if only you could "warp" the rules,and make that tongue longer, bg</td>', 'should win, great image, if only you could "warp" the rules,and make that tongue longer, bg', '2006-02-25 02:24:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181868, 297799, 11923, '<td valign="top">Ha.  I love Bon Jovi.   That''s their best album too!  I like the take off of their album cover.  It looks as if you did an actual writing on wet window? instead of just an image of the album, if so - nicely done.  I like the high contrasty/noisy background too, makes an excellent foil for the lettering.  I gave a 5.</td>', 'Ha.  I love Bon Jovi.   That''s their best album too!  I like the take off of their album cover.  It looks as if you did an actual writing on wet window? instead of just an image of the album, if so - nicely done.  I like the high contrasty/noisy background too, makes an excellent foil for the lettering.  I gave a 5.', '2006-02-25 11:23:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181878, 297636, 11923, '<td valign="top">Mine''s name was Bettina Wendy...  Cute take on the challenge.  Cabbage Patch Kids were certainly all the rage!  I like the environment, the gritty and barren look to it helps further the "hostage" feel.  It feels a little too contrived though for me.  Not sure why, but after the initial, "ha that''s funny/cute" the image doesn''t invite me in to explore - it feels a bit two dimensional, I don''t know how to explain it better, sorry!  That said I did like the environs, the idea is fun, the focus and lighting work well too.  I gave a 5</td>', 'Mine''s name was Bettina Wendy...  Cute take on the challenge.  Cabbage Patch Kids were certainly all the rage!  I like the environment, the gritty and barren look to it helps further the "hostage" feel.  It feels a little too contrived though for me.  Not sure why, but after the initial, "ha that''s funny/cute" the image doesn''t invite me in to explore - it feels a bit two dimensional, I don''t know how to explain it better, sorry!  That said I did like the environs, the idea is fun, the focus and lighting work well too.  I gave a 5', '2006-02-25 11:28:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181888, 297589, 46046, '<td valign="top">very funny! LOL!  LOL is often typed.....I truly laughed out loud.  Very Creative!  The overall compositioni is very good but it bugs me to see the corner of the wall (or whatever is creatinig that shadow).</td>', 'very funny! LOL!  LOL is often typed.....I truly laughed out loud.  Very Creative!  The overall compositioni is very good but it bugs me to see the corner of the wall (or whatever is creatinig that shadow).', '2006-02-25 11:32:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181889, 297642, 11923, '<td valign="top">Wow do those bring back memories.   I like the idea behind the image.  The colors seem a bit muted as does the lighting - maybe it needed a different white balance mode?  Its got a brownish hue to everything.   There are many points of interest to examine which is nice but I''m finding the composition - how they have been laid out to be a bit lacking.  There''s no drama to the image, mostly a flatness that doesn''t draw me in.  It feels more like an image I''d use if I were trying to sell the items on eBay than as an art image I''d put on a wall.   That said, I DO think if there was an adjustment to how the lighting was used (maybe complete darkness with a number of small lights spotlighting each individual item) or if they were arranged in a different manner to give it less of a static feeling then this image could have a greater impact.  I voted a 4.</td>', 'Wow do those bring back memories.   I like the idea behind the image.  The colors seem a bit muted as does the lighting - maybe it needed a different white balance mode?  Its got a brownish hue to everything.   There are many points of interest to examine which is nice but I''m finding the composition - how they have been laid out to be a bit lacking.  There''s no drama to the image, mostly a flatness that doesn''t draw me in.  It feels more like an image I''d use if I were trying to sell the items on eBay than as an art image I''d put on a wall.   That said, I DO think if there was an adjustment to how the lighting was used (maybe complete darkness with a number of small lights spotlighting each individual item) or if they were arranged in a different manner to give it less of a static feeling then this image could have a greater impact.  I voted a 4.', '2006-02-25 11:33:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181893, 297735, 11923, '<td valign="top">A pretty straight-forward image.  Its simple which I like, and each of the headlines brings an spot of interest to the photo.  I think if there had been something different done with the lighting, either to create some unusual shadows or to add a different dimension of contrast, I''d have found the image that much more interesting.  I gave a 4.</td>', 'A pretty straight-forward image.  Its simple which I like, and each of the headlines brings an spot of interest to the photo.  I think if there had been something different done with the lighting, either to create some unusual shadows or to add a different dimension of contrast, I''d have found the image that much more interesting.  I gave a 4.', '2006-02-25 11:35:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181895, 297788, 46046, '<td valign="top">Very nice photograph, love the light on the seawall.  Cyans seem to be pushed a little too high.  That being said,  I think it a stretch to include it in The 80s.  I don''t think a caption (Title in this case) should have to explain a photograph to me.</td>', 'Very nice photograph, love the light on the seawall.  Cyans seem to be pushed a little too high.  That being said,  I think it a stretch to include it in The 80s.  I don''t think a caption (Title in this case) should have to explain a photograph to me.', '2006-02-25 11:36:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181901, 297809, 11923, '<td valign="top">Aww.  I love that movie.   I can''t remember if his chest glows inside on this doll (that''s what it looks like) which if so that can be tough to not get some blown out looking stuff, it also ends up making it look like his chest is gilded a bit which is a tad distracting.  Not sure how that could be adjusted though.   I do like the tact you took for the simple presentation and how his finger and eyes really glow out of the blackness.  I wish there was a skosh more negative space on the right and left though.  When I look at it *I* feel a bit cramped.  The use of light looks good but the focus seems a smidge soft.  I think this would have benefitted from a border too.  I gave a 4.</td>', 'Aww.  I love that movie.   I can''t remember if his chest glows inside on this doll (that''s what it looks like) which if so that can be tough to not get some blown out looking stuff, it also ends up making it look like his chest is gilded a bit which is a tad distracting.  Not sure how that could be adjusted though.   I do like the tact you took for the simple presentation and how his finger and eyes really glow out of the blackness.  I wish there was a skosh more negative space on the right and left though.  When I look at it *I* feel a bit cramped.  The use of light looks good but the focus seems a smidge soft.  I think this would have benefitted from a border too.  I gave a 4.', '2006-02-25 11:39:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181908, 297762, 11923, '<td valign="top">Ha.  Nice shoes.</td>', 'Ha.  Nice shoes.', '2006-02-25 11:40:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181913, 297651, 11923, '<td valign="top">Great presentation, I like the angular, simple feel to the image.  Nice use of a mirror.  Everything looks very clean and crisp for the most part.  I do wish that the colors and the white in the background were just a bit brighter though.  I think if that looked a true bright white, it would''ve made the colors pop and thus the whole image take on an even higher "Wow" factor.  I gave a 6.</td>', 'Great presentation, I like the angular, simple feel to the image.  Nice use of a mirror.  Everything looks very clean and crisp for the most part.  I do wish that the colors and the white in the background were just a bit brighter though.  I think if that looked a true bright white, it would''ve made the colors pop and thus the whole image take on an even higher "Wow" factor.  I gave a 6.', '2006-02-25 11:42:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181914, 297775, 46046, '<td valign="top">Seldomly do I think borders add to a photography....it works here.  Nice color selection.</td>', 'Seldomly do I think borders add to a photography....it works here.  Nice color selection.', '2006-02-25 11:42:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181917, 296923, 11923, '<td valign="top">Nice!  I love the background the most.  Adding in those storm troopers to the back but having them fuzzed out with the shallow DOF really adds to the image in my estimation.  The lighting and focus look great, and I like the composition for the most part.  I do wish though that the hand was either completely in the picture, or the crop was made right before where the fingers on that left side start so we aren''t as "aware" of what we''re missing so it doesn''t grab the eye.   Well done!  I gave a 6.</td>', 'Nice!  I love the background the most.  Adding in those storm troopers to the back but having them fuzzed out with the shallow DOF really adds to the image in my estimation.  The lighting and focus look great, and I like the composition for the most part.  I do wish though that the hand was either completely in the picture, or the crop was made right before where the fingers on that left side start so we aren''t as "aware" of what we''re missing so it doesn''t grab the eye.   Well done!  I gave a 6.', '2006-02-25 11:44:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181922, 297776, 11923, '<td valign="top">Great impact!  How''d ya get the lettering in the ice?   I like the play on the words with the cold/ice and I like how it shows the war''s end with the melting.  The color is not my favorite but I do think it gives the image a boost of drama.  I''m not sure about the lighting.  I feel like the whole image should be completely lit but.. it does work as is.  My favorite portion of the image is the droplet in the "L".  Nice.  I gave a 6.</td>', 'Great impact!  How''d ya get the lettering in the ice?   I like the play on the words with the cold/ice and I like how it shows the war''s end with the melting.  The color is not my favorite but I do think it gives the image a boost of drama.  I''m not sure about the lighting.  I feel like the whole image should be completely lit but.. it does work as is.  My favorite portion of the image is the droplet in the "L".  Nice.  I gave a 6.', '2006-02-25 11:46:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181932, 297588, 11923, '<td valign="top">Hm.. I like the abstract nature of this, but I probably wouldn''t have guessed they were CDs without the title.   Its a very simple image but the coloring with the darkness to the left and the border give it a nice impact.  I even like the muted feel of the neon-ish color.  In the challenge vein, its impact is a bit lessened, but on its own as an abstract picture I do love it.  No idea why there''s a difference, but there is!  I gave a 6.</td>', 'Hm.. I like the abstract nature of this, but I probably wouldn''t have guessed they were CDs without the title.   Its a very simple image but the coloring with the darkness to the left and the border give it a nice impact.  I even like the muted feel of the neon-ish color.  In the challenge vein, its impact is a bit lessened, but on its own as an abstract picture I do love it.  No idea why there''s a difference, but there is!  I gave a 6.', '2006-02-25 11:49:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181942, 297666, 11923, '<td valign="top">Beautiful rose but I''m not seeing a connection to the Prince song really other than the title and thus not seeing the connection to the 80''s.  I even checked the official Purple Rain album cover art to make sure I wasn''t misremembering the imagery on there and thus missing a connection.<br/> <br/>Technically a lovely image, meeting of the challenge, not so much.  I gave a 6 due to the photo itself, had there been some way it met the challenge (in my estimation) I''d have likely given higher.</td>', 'Beautiful rose but I''m not seeing a connection to the Prince song really other than the title and thus not seeing the connection to the 80''s.  I even checked the official Purple Rain album cover art to make sure I wasn''t misremembering the imagery on there and thus missing a connection. Technically a lovely image, meeting of the challenge, not so much.  I gave a 6 due to the photo itself, had there been some way it met the challenge (in my estimation) I''d have likely given higher.', '2006-02-25 11:55:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181953, 296330, 46046, '<td valign="top">This is so 80''s.  Very well done!  I personally would have liked to have her toes.....</td>', 'This is so 80''s.  Very well done!  I personally would have liked to have her toes.....', '2006-02-25 12:00:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2181966, 297508, 46046, '<td valign="top">Excellent!</td>', 'Excellent!', '2006-02-25 12:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2182184, 297694, 40370, '<td valign="top">OMG ... I''d forgotten about that KISS album cover, I spent countless hours drawing that same one after school in the 80''s. Thanks for the memory.</td>', 'OMG ... I''d forgotten about that KISS album cover, I spent countless hours drawing that same one after school in the 80''s. Thanks for the memory.', '2006-02-25 14:11:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2182196, 297441, 40370, '<td valign="top">I won that game once ... final answer was "Constantinople". I like the crispness of you shot, good job digging up an 80''s relic.</td>', 'I won that game once ... final answer was "Constantinople". I like the crispness of you shot, good job digging up an 80''s relic.', '2006-02-25 14:15:28.000000', NULL, 1),
