(2186358, 296930, 27133, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by woohoopepper:</b></div><hr/><i> Wooohoooo, congrats! Let''s face it, if you had done it w/o makeup, it wouldn''t have grabbed much attention, so what you created here is perfect. BTW, what the heck does oi, oi, oi mean????????? I thought it was a Yiddish expression (except that I think that is oy) for being shocked or frustrated. Just can''t be the same thing!!! LOL! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hehehehe...Aussie, Aussie, Aussie, Oi, Oi, Oi...is an Aussie saying...sort of like a chant used at different events, especially sporting events, when we either do well or are trying to encourage a fellow Aussie.  Mainly we use it to show when we are proud.  I hope that makes sense.  In any case....Aussies are seen to be a little nuts....but we are fun loving...hehehe!!<br/> <br/>Thanks so much for your wonderful support everyone...Oi, Oi, Oi....LOL!!</td>', 'Originally posted by woohoopepper: Wooohoooo, congrats! Let''s face it, if you had done it w/o makeup, it wouldn''t have grabbed much attention, so what you created here is perfect. BTW, what the heck does oi, oi, oi mean????????? I thought it was a Yiddish expression (except that I think that is oy) for being shocked or frustrated. Just can''t be the same thing!!! LOL!   Hehehehe...Aussie, Aussie, Aussie, Oi, Oi, Oi...is an Aussie saying...sort of like a chant used at different events, especially sporting events, when we either do well or are trying to encourage a fellow Aussie.  Mainly we use it to show when we are proud.  I hope that makes sense.  In any case....Aussies are seen to be a little nuts....but we are fun loving...hehehe!! Thanks so much for your wonderful support everyone...Oi, Oi, Oi....LOL!!', '2006-02-27 07:38:50.000000', NULL, 0),
